  "body": [
    "Parcel B, Phase 1 of a mixed-use development on the Naugatuck River, designed at WRT Planning + Design for Pennrose. The building turns the corner of Maple Street and Old Firehouse Road to hold both street edges, with retail and the residential lobby at grade and four storeys of apartments above.",
    "The elevations use three families of cladding: a red running-bond brick anchoring the corner, a linen-colored stacked-bond brick along the long west face, and fiber-cement lap siding blended from three greys so the wall reads as texture rather than as panels. A charcoal fiber-cement volume caps the north end, and a stained poplar veneer marks the entrances.",
    "Apartments come in one- and two-bedroom types, each drawn in a Type A and a Type B variant — the first meeting ICC A117.1 and UFAS adaptable requirements, the second the visitable standard — so accessible units are distributed through the building rather than concentrated. Kitchens and bathrooms were drawn as a standard kit and repeated across the types."
  ],
